.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt R-SENT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm r-sent
.Nd simple plaintext presentation tool for Wayland
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Op Ar file
.Op Ar config
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows a presentation described in a plain text file in a single Wayland window,
fullscreen by default.
Every paragraph is one slide.
Text is drawn at the largest font size that fits and centred; images are scaled
to fit and centred.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl \-
End option parsing; the next argument is the file even if it starts with
.Ql - .
.It Ar file
The presentation.
If omitted or
.Ql - ,
the presentation is read from standard input.
.It Ar config
A configuration file whose keys override the defaults (see
.Sx CONFIGURATION ) .
.El
.Sh FILE FORMAT
The file is split into lines; a trailing carriage return is removed and invalid
UTF-8 is replaced by U+FFFD.
.Bl -bullet
.It
An empty line ends the current slide.
Consecutive empty lines collapse.
A line containing only whitespace is content, not a separator.
.It
A line starting with
.Ql #
is a comment and is dropped.
It does not end the current slide.
.It
If the first line of a slide starts with
.Ql @ ,
the slide is an image slide; the rest of the line is the image path, taken
verbatim.
Further lines of an image slide are not drawn.
A line consisting of only
.Ql @
is text.
Relative paths are resolved against the directory containing the presentation
(the current directory for standard input).
.It
One leading backslash is removed from every line, so
.Ql \e@x.png
and
.Ql \e#x
are text lines, and a line consisting of a single backslash is an empty line
(an empty slide).
.El
.Pp
Images are decoded natively (PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, WebP, farbfeld) unless their
path matches a configured filter, in which case the filter command converts
them first.
Transparent images are blended with the background colour.
.Sh KEY AND MOUSE BINDINGS
The default bindings are:
.Bl -tag -width "Right, Return, space, l, j, Down, Next, n"
.It Escape , q
Quit.
.It Right , Return , space , l , j , Down , Next , n
Next slide.
.It Left , BackSpace , h , k , Up , Prior , p
Previous slide.
.It r
Reload the presentation file and its images.
On error the previous presentation is kept.
Not available for standard input.
.It f
Toggle fullscreen.
.It "left button, scroll down"
Next slide.
.It "right button, scroll up"
Previous slide.
.El
.Pp
Keys are matched by the keysym at shift level 0 of the active layout, so
modifiers are ignored.
Holding a key repeats it.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The default configuration is
.Pa config.def.toml
in the source tree.
At build time it is copied to
.Pa config.toml
(if that does not exist), validated and embedded in the binary.
At run time, keys from
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/r-sent/config.toml
(or
.Pa ~/.config/r-sent/config.toml )
and then from the
.Ar config
argument override the embedded configuration.
Tables are merged key by key; the arrays
.Ic fallbacks ,
.Ic keys ,
.Ic mouse
and
.Ic filters
replace the previous array entirely.
Unknown keys are errors.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic fonts.fallbacks
Font families tried in order for every glyph (non-empty).
Characters not covered by any of them are looked up in all installed fonts.
.It Ic fonts.scales , Ic fonts.base_size , Ic fonts.scale_factor
Available font sizes: scale
.Va i
is
.Sy floor(base_size * scale_factor ^ i)
points, for
.Va i
in 0 to scales\-1 (scales 1..256, base_size > 0, scale_factor \(>= 1).
.It Ic colors.foreground , Ic colors.background
Colours as
.Ql #RRGGBB
or
.Ql #RGB .
.It Ic window.fullscreen
Start fullscreen.
.It Ic layout.line_spacing
Distance between baselines as a multiple of the font height (> 0).
.It Ic layout.usable_width , Ic layout.usable_height
Fraction of the window content may use, in (0, 1].
.It Ic keys
Array of
.Brq Ic key , Ic action , Op Ic arg ,
where
.Ic key
is an XKB keysym name.
.It Ic mouse
Array of
.Brq Ic button , Ic action , Op Ic arg ,
where
.Ic button
is one of
.Ql left ,
.Ql middle ,
.Ql right ,
.Ql scroll-up ,
.Ql scroll-down .
.It Ic filters
Array of
.Brq Ic regex , Ic command .
The first filter whose regex matches the image path (case-insensitively) is
used: the command is run with
.Ql sh -c ,
receives the image on standard input and must write an image to standard
output.
.El
.Pp
Actions are
.Ql quit ,
.Ql advance
(with an integer
.Ic arg
giving the number of slides to move),
.Ql reload
and
.Ql toggle-fullscreen .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Fatal errors are printed as a single line starting with
.Ql r-sent:\& .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
r-sent

@diagram.png

why plain text
- diffable
- no tooling
# comment, not shown
\e# shown, starts with a hash
.Ed
.Pp
Show a presentation, or one generated on the fly:
.Dl $ r-sent talk.txt
.Dl $ printf 'hello\en\enworld\en' | r-sent
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sent 1
